# Subscription System

**Last updated:** August 2026
**Verified against:** `lib/config/subscriptions.ts`, `lib/config/packages.ts`, `prisma/schema.prisma`
**Status:** Fully implemented and working

---

## Overview

DriveBook uses a 4-tier subscription model for providers. Subscriptions are managed via Stripe. The system handles trials, upgrades, downgrades, billing portal, and post-portal sync.

A 5th tier (BUSINESS — multi-provider) is displayed in the UI as "Coming Soon" but has no backend implementation and no Stripe price IDs.

---

## Active Tiers

Source of truth: `lib/config/subscriptions.ts` → `SUBSCRIPTION_PLANS`

| Tier | Monthly | Annual | Commission | Trial | Status |
|------|---------|--------|------------|-------|--------|
| BASIC | $29 | $290 | 15% | 14 days | Live |
| PRO | $79 | $790 | 12% | 14 days | Live |
| STUDIO | $129 | $1,290 | 11% | 14 days | Live |
| PREMIUM | $199 | $1,990 | 10% | 30 days | Live |
| BUSINESS | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD | Coming Soon |

**PREMIUM** is the 4th active tier — renamed from BUSINESS in August 2026. It is for **single providers** with full white-label and direct payment capability (direct payments are phase 2 — see below).

**BUSINESS** tier is a future multi-provider tier (unlimited providers, role-based access, school-level branding). It is shown in the subscription UI with a "Coming Soon" badge. There is no `SUBSCRIPTION_PLANS.BUSINESS` key and no Stripe price IDs for it.

Note: The `newStudentBonus` concept was removed May 2026. Commission is a flat rate per tier.

---

## Commission Rate Source

Commission rates are read from `PlatformSettings` DB record at payment creation time via `lib/services/platform-pricing.ts → getCommissionRate(tier)`.

Internal DB field names:
- `basicCommissionRate` → BASIC tier
- `proCommissionRate` → PRO tier
- `studioCommissionRate` → STUDIO tier
- `businessCommissionRate` → PREMIUM tier (field name unchanged for DB compatibility; also serves any future BUSINESS tier until it has its own rate)

The rate is locked on the booking at creation time — never re-derived at payout time.

Config fallback: `lib/config/packages.ts` → `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` defines hardcoded defaults used when no DB record exists:
```typescript
basicCommissionRate: 15,
proCommissionRate: 12,
studioCommissionRate: 11,
businessCommissionRate: 10,  // serves PREMIUM tier
```

---

## Tier Feature Matrix

Source of truth: `lib/config/subscriptions.ts` → `SUBSCRIPTION_PLANS[tier].limits`

| Feature | BASIC | PRO | STUDIO | PREMIUM |
|---------|-------|-----|--------|---------|
| Max providers | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 |
| Custom domain | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Branded pages | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Priority support | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| API access | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |

**Multi-provider management** is NOT in any active tier. It is planned for the future BUSINESS tier.

**Direct payments (0% commission)** is listed as a PREMIUM feature but is NOT yet implemented. All payments currently route through the DriveBook Stripe account (PLATFORM mode). The guard is in `lib/utils/account.ts → assertPlatformPaymentMode()` which throws a runtime error if `paymentMode=DIRECT` is set on any account.

---

## Payment Mode

Two payment modes exist on the `Provider` schema:
- `PLATFORM` (default) — all payments flow through DriveBook Stripe
- `DIRECT` — payments go to provider's own Stripe account via Stripe Connect

**DIRECT mode is phase 2 and not yet implemented.** Any account set to `paymentMode=DIRECT` will throw an error at checkout. Do not set this value manually.

---

## DB Models

### `Provider` model (subscription fields)

From `prisma/schema.prisma`:
```prisma
subscriptionTier    String    @default("BASIC")   // BASIC | PRO | STUDIO | PREMIUM
subscriptionStatus  String    @default("TRIAL")   // TRIAL | ACTIVE | PAST_DUE | CANCELLED
trialEndsAt         DateTime?
stripeCustomerId    String?
stripeAccountId     String?
paymentMode         String    @default("PLATFORM") // PLATFORM | DIRECT (DIRECT = phase 2)
businessModel       String    @default("SAAS")     // MARKETPLACE | SAAS
```

### `Subscription` model

```prisma
id                   String
providerId           String
tier                 String    // BASIC | PRO | STUDIO | PREMIUM
status               String    @default("ACTIVE")
billingCycle         String    @default("monthly")
monthlyAmount        Float
stripeSubscriptionId String?
stripeCustomerId     String?
currentPeriodStart   DateTime
currentPeriodEnd     DateTime
cancelAtPeriodEnd    Boolean   @default(false)
trialEndsAt          DateTime?
cancelledAt          DateTime?
```

### `PlatformRateChange` model

```prisma
id            String
tier          String    // BASIC | PRO | STUDIO | PREMIUM | ALL
field         String    // basicCommissionRate | proCommissionRate | studioCommissionRate | businessCommissionRate
currentRate   Float
newRate       Float
effectiveDate DateTime
reason        String
status        String    @default("PENDING")  // PENDING | APPLIED | CANCELLED
notifiedAt    DateTime?
appliedAt     DateTime?
createdBy     String
```

Note: The `businessCommissionRate` field name serves the PREMIUM tier. There is no separate `premiumCommissionRate` DB column.

---

## Stripe Price IDs

From `lib/config/subscriptions.ts → STRIPE_PRICE_IDS`:
```typescript
BASIC_MONTHLY, BASIC_ANNUAL
PRO_MONTHLY, PRO_ANNUAL
STUDIO_MONTHLY, STUDIO_ANNUAL
PREMIUM_MONTHLY, PREMIUM_ANNUAL
```

Environment variables:
```
STRIPE_BASIC_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID
STRIPE_PRO_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID
STRIPE_STUDIO_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID
STRIPE_PREMIUM_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID   # was STRIPE_BUSINESS_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID before rename
STRIPE_PREMIUM_ANNUAL_PRICE_ID
```

---

## APIs

| Method | Route | Description |
|--------|-------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/instructor/subscription` | Current subscription + all plan definitions |
| POST | `/api/instructor/subscription` | Create trial or change tier during trial |
| DELETE | `/api/instructor/subscription` | Cancel subscription (sets cancelAtPeriodEnd) |
| POST | `/api/instructor/subscription/billing-portal` | Open Stripe Billing Portal (active) or Checkout (trial) |
| POST | `/api/instructor/subscription/sync` | Sync state from Stripe after portal return |
| POST | `/api/instructor/subscription/mobile` | Mobile app tier selection |
| GET | `/api/admin/rate-changes` | List scheduled rate changes |
| POST | `/api/admin/rate-changes` | Schedule a rate change |
| DELETE | `/api/admin/rate-changes/[id]` | Cancel pending rate change |
| GET | `/api/cron/apply-rate-changes` | Apply due rate changes (daily cron) |

---

## Upgrade/Downgrade Flow

**Trial providers:** `POST /api/instructor/subscription` with new tier. DB updated immediately. Trial end date preserved.

**Active paid providers:** `POST /api/instructor/subscription/billing-portal` → Stripe Billing Portal → return with `?portal_return=true` → `POST /api/instructor/subscription/sync` pulls latest state from Stripe.

Webhook (`customer.subscription.updated`) also fires as a second DB update. Tier is derived from the Stripe price ID when metadata is missing (handles Billing Portal upgrades). Price ID → tier mapping lives in all webhook handlers.

---

## Stripe Webhook Events Handled

| Event | Handler |
|-------|---------|
| `customer.subscription.created` | `handleSubscriptionUpdate` — creates/updates Subscription record |
| `customer.subscription.updated` | `handleSubscriptionUpdate` — syncs tier, status, period |
| `customer.subscription.deleted` | `handleSubscriptionCancelled` — sets status CANCELLED |
| `customer.subscription.trial_will_end` | `handleTrialEnding` — sends 3-day warning email |
| `invoice.payment_succeeded` | `handleInvoicePaymentSucceeded` — sets status ACTIVE |
| `invoice.payment_failed` | `handleInvoicePaymentFailed` — sets status PAST_DUE |

---

## Scheduled Rate Changes

Admins schedule rate changes via `/admin/pricing → Rate Change Scheduler`. The `apply-rate-changes` cron applies them on the effective date and notifies all affected providers.

---

## What Is NOT Implemented (Phase 2)

- **DIRECT payment mode** — `paymentMode=DIRECT` throws a runtime error. Do not use.
- **BUSINESS tier** — no `SUBSCRIPTION_PLANS.BUSINESS` key, no Stripe price IDs, no backend routes. UI shows "Coming Soon".
- **Multi-provider management** — all tiers have `providers: 1`. No account can have multiple providers.
- **0% commission** — PREMIUM tier lists this as a future feature; it requires DIRECT mode which is phase 2.
